identifier: kgmicrobe.ingredient:demineralized_water
preferred_term: Demineralized water
mapping_status: MAPPED
ingredient_type: SINGLE_INGREDIENT
synonyms:
- synonym_text: Demineralized water
  synonym_type: EXACT_SYNONYM
  source: mediadive.ingredient:1448; original DSMZ1191/1279/1600/1793
ontology_mapping:
  ontology_id: CHEBI:15377
  ontology_label: water
  ontology_source: CHEBI
  mapping_quality: NARROW_MATCH
  evidence:
  - evidence_type: LLM_SUGGESTION
    source: https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium1191.pdf
    notes: The source grade demineralized water is explicitly named in all nine admitted
      ingredient1448 rows across DSMZ1191,1279,1600 and1793, including the source
      abbreviations H2O demin. and Aqua dem. It is represented as a distinct preparation-qualified
      solvent, with CHEBI15377 water as a broader molecular parent only. No ion-removal
      method, conductivity, resistivity, reagent standard, quantitative purity or
      universal sterility is asserted. The one sterile addition in DSMZ1600 retains
      that operational qualifier in its recipe; this owner does not globally equate
      sterile water, distilled water or tap water. The exact-name OLS search found
      TransformON c_ROHSUO, but TFO is outside the maintained OntologySourceEnum and
      its conductivity scope is not specified by these sources; the candidate is preserved
      as context rather than silently adopted or reported absent.
supplied_form:
- name: Demineralized water
  form: preparation-qualified water
  notes: Source specifies the demineralized grade but no quantitative specification
    or treatment route. Sterility is occurrence-specific.
